  "doctrine": [
    {
      "topic": "rainbow-covenant",
      "statement": "God sets the rainbow in the clouds as the sign of his covenant with Noah and every living creature that a flood will never again destroy all flesh.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "ref": "Gen.9.11",
          "role": "defining",
          "note": "The promise concerns all flesh and the earth."
        },
        {
          "ref": "Gen.9.16",
          "role": "defining",
          "note": "God sees the bow and remembers the everlasting covenant."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "note": "The corpus groups the bow and archer with קשש ‘gather stubble’. The final taw and the comparative forms support treating the bow family separately. The Maltese and Arabic rainbow compounds and the Mandaic expression show how the bow noun can be qualified to denote the sky phenomenon."
